  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), giving us a weak RNA-only baseline and essentially no information about whether the image modality is informative. Uncertainty: The most critical open question is whether image features carry complementary or superior signal relative to RNA. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the modality effect by matching config_001 on profile_setting (singleprofile) while switching to the simplest image encoder (resnet50). This is a clean single-variable comparison (RNA vs. image modality). Why this is the best next step: Under a tight budget, knowing whether image is a viable modality determines the entire downstream search strategy—if image is strong, we prioritize image/multimodal configs; if weak, we focus on RNA encoder and profile improvements. Testing a multimodal config now would confound modality, fusion, and aggregation effects, making the result harder to interpret. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-leverage design decision."
}

